# Prospektor

> You spend about three minutes teaching Prospektor what your company is and
> what you are hunting for — new customers, distribution partners, resellers,
> companies worth investing in or acquiring. It then finds those companies,
> names the person at each one worth contacting, and writes what you send them.
> The writing is the product: a deck, a one-pager, emails and a proposal in one
> client's voice, grounded in the work that client has already won.

This domain is the marketing site: what the product is, and what it costs. The
application is `studio.prospektor.ai`, and it has its own file for machines —
[studio.prospektor.ai/llms.txt](https://studio.prospektor.ai/llms.txt) lists the
calls that need no account. Nothing on this domain is an API.

## The price

US$999 a month, per workspace, paid before you start. A workspace is one company
you are selling for, so an agency selling for five clients keeps five. Runs are
unlimited and every colleague on your work-email domain is included — no seats to
count, no credit meter. Money back if it doesn't earn its keep.
[prospektor.ai/pricing/](https://prospektor.ai/pricing/) answers the rest of the
money questions.

## What it does

**Who to pitch** — it reads a company's own site, scores it against your brief,
and names the same-named companies it ruled out. Your brief decides what counts
as a target, so the same machinery hunts customers, channel partners, resellers,
investment targets or acquisitions. **What to send** — the deck, the one-pager,
the emails and the proposal, in your voice, grounded in work you have already
won. The second half is the hard one, and it is what you are paying for.

The setup is short and happens once: naming your company creates the workspace,
the studio reads your site and drafts the brief, and you correct it by answering
a few questions. Nothing has to be re-explained afterwards.

Five agents do the run, and each one shows its work. The names are the sales-org
job titles the work corresponds to, in plain terms:

- **BDR** — *the researcher.* Brings companies worth approaching, scored against your brief.
- **SDR** — *the door-opener.* Decision-makers with a source behind every name, then who in your network can introduce you.
- **AE** — *the writer.* Writes the deck, the one-pager, the proposal and the emails.
- **Sales Ops** — *the fact-checker.* Checks the work before you see it: an invented number, a fabricated person, a ruled-out company.
- **RevOps** — *the memory.* Remembers what worked, so run 100 is not run 1.

There is no scheduled hunt — nothing goes looking on a timer. What keeps the
queue full is that the studio offers three companies before you ask for any,
every run ends with more like the one it just did, and a batch takes up to 100
companies while the tab is closed.

They research, draft and check. You send — nothing signs your name but you. The
two halves in full: [prospektor.ai/who-to-pitch/](https://prospektor.ai/who-to-pitch/)
and [prospektor.ai/what-to-send/](https://prospektor.ai/what-to-send/).

